'''Bayani Baliscans''' ({{Lang-bl|Bayano-baliscanos}}; {{Langx|ar|البيان في باليسكان|al-bayān fī bālīskān}}) are [[Baliscans]] of predominantly [[Bayanis|Bayani ancestry]]. People from the [[Bayani world]] arrived in [[Balisca]] as early as the beginning of the 16th century, during the [[colonization of Balisca]]. Historically, those considered "Bayani" in Balisca included [[W:Turkish people|Turks]], [[W:Moors|Moors]], [[W:Berbers|Mauretanians]], [[W:Syrian people|"Syrians"]], "[[W:Lebanese people|Lebanese]]", and "[[W:Palestinians|Palestinians]]". Bayani Baliscans are the largest [[W:Arab diaspora|Bayani diaspora]] in the world. 

It is estimated that 28 million Baliscan are chiefly descendants of immigrants from the Bayani world (i.e., [[W:Palestinians|Palestinians]], [[W:Syrians|Syrians]], [[W:Lebanese people|Lebanese]], and Middle East [[W:Armenians|Armenians]]). Roughly 3,000,000 of these are Palestinian descendants. It is one of the largest Palestinian communities outside of the Arab world. Many of them are descendants from Christian immigrants from several places in Central Fosia. The earliest such migrants came in the 1850s, with others arriving during and after the [[Great Adonian War]].

Bayani Baliscans have been an influential group in Baliscan society since the colonial era and especially since the [[Espanya Boba|''Andalusya Boba'']] period, playing an important role in the shaping of Baliscan culture and [[Foreign relations of Balisca|international policy]]. 

